  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Using the source's exact-form convention, an exponential function must have the form \\(y=a^x\\), where \\(a>0\\) and \\(a\\ne1\\). Only \\(y=2^x\\) has this form, so the answer under that convention is B. \\(y=2^x+1\\) is a translation of an exponential function.\n\nUnder a broader convention that includes vertical translates, both B and D qualify. Because the English question does not state the convention, it has no convention-independent unique choice.",
